        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CtbqzY2CMxK35j-hzqa_-47" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Search with From, To&amp;nbsp; dates of travel etc:&lt;div&gt;The searching will be on specific query pattern and is of higher numbers than the writes to train seats. So cassandra makes sense to be used here.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="330" x="10" y="511.26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CtbqzY2CMxK35j-hzqa_-48" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Strong consistency in seat booking :&lt;div&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-start=&quot;118&quot; data-end=&quot;412&quot;&gt;Redis will be used as a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;142&quot; data-end=&quot;185&quot;&gt;temporary coordinator for seat capacity&lt;/strong&gt;. For a booking request, we check whether the available seat count is sufficient for the requested number of seats. If sufficient capacity exists, Redis performs an &lt;strong data-start=&quot;350&quot; data-end=&quot;370&quot;&gt;atomic decrement&lt;/strong&gt; to reserve the requested number of seats.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-start=&quot;414&quot; data-end=&quot;576&quot;&gt;The temporary reservation is maintained with a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;461&quot; data-end=&quot;468&quot;&gt;TTL&lt;/strong&gt;, so if the booking flow fails or is abandoned, the reservation can expire and the capacity can be released.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-start=&quot;578&quot; data-end=&quot;815&quot;&gt;For concurrent requests, the availability check and decrement must be &lt;strong data-start=&quot;648&quot; data-end=&quot;658&quot;&gt;atomic&lt;/strong&gt;. For example, if 2 seats are available and two users simultaneously request 2 seats, only one request can successfully decrement the count; the other fails.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="231.26" width="430" x="360" y="650" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CtbqzY2CMxK35j-hzqa_-49" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;Hot Events:&lt;br&gt;Break this into two part Lookup and booking&lt;br&gt;For lookup:&lt;br&gt;The Hot events fetch will go through the redis to fasten up and save effort on search.&lt;br&gt;For booking:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;we will enable the processing through booking queue and the flow can be controlled with back pressure.&lt;br&gt;We enable the confirmation with SSE to fetch booking status.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="370" x="806" y="661.26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CtbqzY2CMxK35j-hzqa_-50" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Payments:&lt;br&gt;Usually the payments are docoupled but for this sytem we integrated with the booking service for simplicity. But the Payments will be done asynchronously and the update from payments will be done with the Webhook.&lt;br&gt;Idempotency of the payment to be ensured with booking ID and the retry to analyse the state before processing a new payment. This avoid the duplicate charging for user." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="330" x="1190" y="661.26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CtbqzY2CMxK35j-hzqa_-53" parent="1" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=15;" value="cassandra&lt;br&gt;JourneyDB" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="70" x="1180" y="30.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
